a rect can be converted between user and device space

-[O2GState convertRectToDeviceSpace:] and its user space twin were both O2UnimplementedMethod
returning O2RectZero, while the point and size conversions beside them have been implemented all
along against the same _deviceSpaceTransform.

This is not a theoretical gap. Money Manager EX imports _CGContextConvertRectToDeviceSpace, and
before this its app log carried thousands of the unimplemented line per draw, every one of them an
answer of CGRectZero to a question about a real rectangle.

ALL FOUR CORNERS, then the bounding box, which is what CGRectApplyAffineTransform documents.
Transforming the origin and the size separately agrees with that only while the transform neither
rotates nor shears, and hands back a negative width the moment it flips, which is exactly the shape
of transform a flipped view installs.

MEASURED: the unimplemented line is gone, 0 of thousands. NOTHING VISIBLE CHANGED in the scenario
that provoked it: the mmex User Interface Language dialog is pixel identical before and after, and
its list box is still empty, which is #213 and is not this.
